{%- comment -%}
  Selected projects — the B2B proof. Brief §8 and §9.3.

  THIS SECTION WAS REFUSED ONCE, AND THE REASON IT IS BUILT NOW IS THAT THE
  REASON CHANGED. On 2026-08-31 it was decided not to build it for v1: the brief
  asks for a portfolio and forbids inflating one, and there were no project
  photographs and no nameable clients, so an empty portfolio was worse than no
  portfolio. On 2026-09-13 the studio handed over four pieces of real work —
  a hospital uniform programme, an institutional shirt, a corporate two-tone
  shirt and a canvas tote — and the objection went with them.

  What has NOT changed is the rule underneath it. There is still no "trusted by
  hundreds of companies", no invented client list, and no project here that the
  studio did not make. Adding a fifth means adding a photograph, not a sentence.

  CLIENT NAMES ARE A SETTING AND THREE OF THEM ARE BLANK ON PURPOSE. The studio
  authorised naming clients on 2026-09-13. Only one name could actually be read
  off the photographs with certainty — Salna, embroidered front and back on the
  corporate shirt. The hospital programme and the institutional shirt carry their
  clients' names in embroidery a few pixels tall, and a client name guessed from
  a blurry crop and then published is exactly the class of invention this repo
  refuses. So those render the labelled placeholder until the studio types them
  in, which is a theme-editor edit and not a code change.

  THE PHOTOGRAPHS ARE CUT OUT, AND THAT CHANGED THE WHOLE BLOCK ON 2026-09-13.
  They arrived as studio shots on white and light-grey sweeps, and dropped onto
  this site they read as four foreign rectangles: the page is #fdfaf7 and the
  band is #fbf4ef, both warm, and a cold paper white next to them looks like a
  screenshot of somebody else's website. The studio's words were "gk masuk ke
  theme warna shopify store kita".

  So each one now carries an alpha matte and the garment sits on the site's own
  surface. Three consequences, all of them deliberate:

  - **They are `contain`, not `cover`.** A cut-out cropped to fill a box has its
    sleeves cut off by nothing. Each object sits inside its frame whole, at its
    own proportions — 1.62 for the institutional pair, 0.96 for the tote — and
    the FRAME is what stays consistent, not the subject.
  - **They sit on a PLATE, one surface step up from the band.** Not on tone,
    which is the placeholder's colour and would put a taupe rectangle back
    behind every garment. The plate follows the three-deep stack in CLAUDE.md:
    cream when the band is plain page, white when the band is cream, so the
    object always has exactly one step of separation and never flattens into
    whatever it is sitting on.
  - **The plate is generously padded.** A cut-out touching the edge of its own
    box looks like a failed crop rather than an object on a surface.

  How the mattes were made, because it is not the obvious way and the obvious
  way fails: the background is flood-filled INWARDS FROM THE FRAME EDGE, so what
  decides a pixel is whether it connects to the border, not whether it matches a
  colour. A global colour key on these would have eaten the two white hospital
  uniforms and the off-white canvas tote, which are the same value as the paper
  behind them; connectivity saves them, because the navy trim and the piping
  close the path. The masters are untouched in `asset/B2B Project/`.

  THE BAND COLOUR IS A SETTING, AND IT EXISTS BECAUSE THIS SECTION MOVES. Cream
  is the default and it is what the section wants on its own: a step away from
  the plain page above it and away from an espresso band below.

  What forced the setting is the home page's Custom & business view, where this
  section sits directly above `custom-band`, which is cream and argues at length
  for staying cream. Two cream bands touching read as one long cream region with
  a seam in it — the same rule, from the other side. So there it is set to plain
  page and `custom-band` keeps the cream.

  Neither value may be espresso. On any template where the voices wall is below,
  espresso here would put two dark bands against each other, which is the
  original form of the same mistake.

  NO COUNTS, NO YEARS, NO LOGOS. A "since 2019" or a client logo wall is the
  cheapest way to inflate a portfolio of four, and the brief forbids exactly
  that. The detail line under each project says what is in the photograph and
  nothing the photograph does not show.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The padding moves with the tone, and forgetting that is how this section got
  a 180px hole under the home page's tab bar on its first build. A band pays
  for its own top margin AND its inside padding, because the colour change is
  what has to be separated from its neighbours. A section that is just page
  does not: it wants one `pt-section` and nothing else, exactly like
  `new-arrivals` directly above it in the other view.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if section.settings.tone == 'page'
    assign band = 'pt-section'
    assign pad = ''
  else
    assign band = 'mt-section border-y border-rule bg-canvas'
    assign pad = 'py-section'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The plate is one step up from whatever the band is, never the same as it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if section.settings.tone == 'page'
    assign plate = 'bg-canvas'
  else
    assign plate = 'bg-surface'
  endif
-%}

<section
  aria-labelledby="projects-heading"
  class="{{ band }}"
>
  <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-10 px-gutter {{ pad }}">
    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <span class="text-micro uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-subtle">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.eyebrow, label: 'eyebrow', inline: true %}
      </span>

      <h2 id="projects-heading" class="text-h1 leading-h1">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
      </h2>

      <p class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body, label: 'description', lines: 2 %}
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="grid gap-x-6 gap-y-10 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <li data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="{{ plate }} rounded-sm p-7 sm:p-9">
              {% render 'media-asset',
                image: block.settings.image,
                asset: block.settings.asset,
                alt: block.settings.alt,
                ratio: '4 / 3',
                fit: 'contain',
                plate: false,
                asset_width: 1200,
                asset_height: 900,
                sizes: '(min-width: 640px) 42vw, 84vw',
                label: 'Project photo' %}
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
              {%- comment -%}
                The client's name is the heading, not the category. A portfolio
                entry titled "Hospital uniforms" is a service; one titled with
                the hospital's name is a job somebody actually commissioned, and
                that difference is the entire reason this section exists.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <h3 class="text-h3 leading-h3">
                {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.client, label: 'client', inline: true %}
              </h3>

              <p class="text-caption uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
                {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.category, label: 'category', inline: true %}
              </p>

              <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
                {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.detail, label: 'detail', inline: true %}
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.cta != blank -%}
      <div data-reveal class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        {% render 'button',
          label: section.settings.cta,
          href: section.settings.href,
          variant: 'primary',
          class: 'max-sm:w-full px-6 sm:px-11' %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Selected projects",
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Real work only. A project here needs a photograph of something the studio actually produced — do not add an entry to lengthen the list, and do not add client counts, years or logos. The detail line should say what the photograph shows and nothing more." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "tone", "label": "Band", "default": "cream", "options": [
      { "value": "cream", "label": "Cream band" },
      { "value": "page", "label": "Plain page" }
    ], "info": "Cream unless the section directly below is also cream. Two cream bands touching read as one." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Custom apparel" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Selected projects" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Description", "default": "Uniforms, corporate apparel and merchandise produced for organisations across Indonesia." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Button" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta", "label": "Label", "default": "Discuss your project" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "href", "label": "Link" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "project",
      "name": "Project",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "client", "label": "Client", "info": "The organisation the work was made for. Type it only if the studio has their agreement to name them — leave it blank and a labelled placeholder renders rather than a guess." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "category", "label": "Category" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "detail", "label": "Detail", "info": "One line about what the photograph shows." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Overrides the shipped asset below." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "asset", "label": "Shipped asset filename" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text", "info": "Used by the shipped asset only." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Selected projects" }]
}
{% endschema %}
